# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-16, R-6, RC-5; L §5.19 Readings at a place that keeps parts). L §5.19 A pad: "at x it is an arrival, labelled by the arrival rule (a cited house reading of the
# gap, or a written ? rule that makes it a hole part, §8.1)". The end-of-month pad of 30.00 is tomek's by rule pad
# (scratch/exp7.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
  rule pad beats base, t = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in pads
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-01
  pad konto from world
  stated[konto] = 130.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
=== expect
q: (130.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN)
  pad: konto 2026-03-31 end, pads:stmt:konto@2026-03-31 end of 30.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: a1
  cut 2026-10-01
